<title>CANADA: Bank of Canada 91-day T-bill yields avg 2.852 pct.</title>
<headline>Bank of Canada 91-day T-bill yields avg 2.852 pct.</headline>
<dateline>OTTAWA 1997-01-07</dateline>
<text>
<p>The Bank of Canada said on Tuesday the average yield at this week's auction of C$2.5 billion of 91-day Government of Canada treasury bills due April 10 was 2.852 percent, up from 2.799 percent last week.</p>
<p>The average yield on C$1.2 billion of 175-day T-bills due July 3, 1997 was 3.292 percent, up from 3.176 percent last week, and on C$1.1 billion of 364-day T-bills due January 8, 1998 was 3.747 percent, up from 3.541 percent.</p>
<p>The Bank bought C$500 million three-month, C$150 million six-month and C$150 million one-year bills. It holds C$1.0 billion of C$6.0 billion bills due January 16. (Details follow)  </p>
